  :issued (1994 11 23) :issued-uri "https://www.gov.za/sites/default/files/gcis_document/201409/act36of1994.pdf" :published (1994 12 7) :published-uri "https://www.gov.za/sites/default/files/gcis_document/201409/act36of1994.pdf" :published-in "Government Gazette Vol. 354 No. 16136, 7 December 1994 (Notice 2088 of 1994)" :in-force (1995 1 1) :summary "Schedule 1: 12 public holidays — 1 Jan New Year's Day, 21 Mar Human Rights Day, Good Friday (Friday before Easter Sunday), Family Day (Monday after Easter Sunday), 27 Apr Freedom Day, 1 May Workers' Day, 16 Jun Youth Day, 9 Aug National Women's Day, 24 Sep Heritage Day, 16 Dec Day of Reconciliation, 25 Dec Christmas Day, 26 Dec Day of Goodwill. s. 2(1): a public holiday falling on a Sunday makes the following Monday a public holiday. s. 6: commencement 1 January 1995. Repeals the Public Holidays Act 5 of 1952.")
